      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm transition hover:shadow-md">
        <div class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Acts safely in a sandbox</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Agents run in containers scoped to a project workspace. They see only the tools you
          grant and nothing more — no exfiltration, no arbitrary endpoints, no cross-project
          secrets.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm transition hover:shadow-md">
        <div class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m-6 9l2 2 4-4" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Under audit, with approval gates</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Every retrieval, tool call, and model call is logged. High-risk actions pause for
          explicit human sign-off via approval cards showing the exact diff, SQL, or command.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── FIVE CORE CONCEPTS ─────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="border-y border-slate-100 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 md:px-10">
      <h2 class="text-center text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-4xl">
        Built around five core concepts
      </h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
        Myrmec sits between your people and your AI models. Admins set up the platform once;
        everyone else just uses it.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {concepts.map((c) => (
          <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">{c.desc}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
        <article class="flex flex-col justify-center rounded-2xl border border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50/60 p-6 text-center">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700">DevOps owns the infra.</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700">Business owns the tasks.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── HOW EXECUTION WORKS ────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 md:px-10">
    <h2 class="text-center text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-4xl">How work gets done</h2>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-500">Workflows</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Deterministic, step by step</h3>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-indigo-400">→</span>A sequence of steps, each assigned to an agent profile with its own input, output, and acceptance criteria.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-indigo-400">→</span>Trigger an execution and watch a live view stream logs and step-level status in real time.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-indigo-400">→</span>Every result and log line persisted — audit behaviour, rerun failed steps, never lose history.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-500">Assistants</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Conversational, real time</h3>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-indigo-400">→</span>Pick a published assistant and start chatting — configuration is the admin's job, not yours.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-indigo-400">→</span>Token-by-token streaming shows thinking, tool calls, and citations as they happen.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-indigo-400">→</span>Risky actions pause behind approval cards; sessions are persistent, shareable, and fully recorded.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── FEATURES GRID ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="border-y border-slate-100 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 md:px-10">
      <h2 class="text-center text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-4xl">
        Everything a governed agent platform needs
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {features.map((g) => (
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">{g.group}</h3>
            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4">
              {g.items.map(([title, desc]) => (
                <li>
                  <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">{title}</p>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-500">{desc}</p>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── WHY MYRMEC ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 md:px-10">
    <h2 class="text-center text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-4xl">Why teams choose Myrmec</h2>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">The CISO conversation, solved by design</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Regulated industries can't use laptop copilots because of data egress and audit
          requirements. Myrmec sandboxes every agent, encrypts credentials inside the platform,
          supports on-prem and air-gapped model providers, and logs every action.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Institutional memory, not private prompts</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          In most companies AI knowledge lives in a developer's private chat history. Myrmec
          captures prompt engineering and system logic into agent profiles that belong to the
          organisation — permanently.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">No model lock-in</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Agent profiles are decoupled from specific models. Switching providers is a
          configuration change, not a code change — mix local Ollama with cloud OpenAI in the
          same deployment if you want.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Deterministic outcomes from non-deterministic models</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Structured agentic flows force the AI to follow a defined process, greatly increasing
          the reliability of the output versus free-form prompting.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

